      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part I, Line 1:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Program development and delivery that facilitates leadership development at the individual, group/organization, and community level throughout San Diego County, specifically to support the region's underserved and underrepresented communities to elevate meaningful, community-centered leadership. These programs fall into three pillars or focus areas: leadership development that uses an adaptive leadership framework that empowers individuals to tackle seemingly intractable challenges in and with their communities; civic engagement that fosters critical dialogue and resident-led action around issues impacting urban communities throughout San Diego County; and nonprofit partnerships that strengthen nonprofits and social enterprises through technical assistance and training to facilitate and promote a culture of collective impact. Programming primarily consists of intensive fellowship opportunities designed for adults and youth at the high school and college level, moderated community discussions with community experts, and trainings and technical assistance opportunities for nonprofit staff, board members, and volunteers.</ExplanationTxt>
